`ProvidersSection._addProvider` (the canonical Settings → Providers → Add flow, providers_section.dart:385) constructs `AddProviderPresetPickerPage` directly via `pushFaPage`, and flutter_app's host builder (providers_section.dart:138) builds its own instance too. Those are the *destination* of the routing, not routers — correct as-is, but the doc's "every … routes through this helper" will read as false to the next reader who greps for direct constructions.

Reword to scope the claim to the routing decision, e.g.:

```dart
/// Every host-or-fallback ROUTING of the add-provider flow goes through
/// this helper; adding a knob happens once, here. (The canonical
/// Settings → Providers → Add entry is the destination, not a router.)
```
